  "blocks": [
    {
      "block_id": 0,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "The WAIT Instruction\n",
      "bbox": [
        85.55000305175781,
        85.15818786621094,
        239.19505310058594,
        100.15818786621094
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.1423863665569247,
        0.11032568187737903,
        0.3981076948504363,
        0.12975875425276373
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 1,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "The WAIT instruction causes the Copper to wait until the video beam counters are equal to (or \ngreater than) the coordinates specified in the instruction. While waiting, the Copper is off the bus \nand not using memory cycles.\n",
      "bbox": [
        85.30000305175781,
        127.97502899169922,
        517.9735107421875,
        163.82305908203125
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.14197027549474558,
        0.16579653337584319,
        0.8620965930614174,
        0.21223902425986926
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 2,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "The first instruction word contains the vertical and horizontal coordinates of the beam position. \nThe second word contains enable bits that are used to form a “ mask\" that tells the system which \nbits of the beam position to use in making the comparison.\n",
      "bbox": [
        85.55000305175781,
        178.9720458984375,
        517.761474609375,
        215.364013671875
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.1423863665569247,
        0.2318651147410007,
        0.8617436877025282,
        0.2790122976492593
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 3,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "FIRST INSTRUCTION WORD (IR1)\n",
